---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { operator, support } from '../../data/payment';
---

<Base
  title="Refund and cancellation policy"
  description="When Rsquared Academy refunds paid access, how to ask, and how long a refund takes."
>
  <section class="sec page-head" aria-labelledby="refund-h">
    <div class="wrap legal">
      <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
      <h1 id="refund-h" class="t-h1">Refund and cancellation policy</h1>
      <p class="t-small t-muted">Last updated: 11 November 2026</p>
      <p>{operator.line}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec flush" aria-labelledby="policy-h">
    <div class="wrap legal">
      <h2 id="policy-h" class="t-h3">12-month pass: refunds within 14 days</h2>
      <p>For a 12-month pass, you can ask for a full refund within 14 days of purchase if you have completed less than 20% of the lessons in every paid track (no single track at 20% or more). Your account page shows your progress in each track.</p>
      <p>After 14 days, or once you have completed 20% or more of the lessons in any paid track, we do not refund, except for duplicate charges, failed access we cannot fix within 7 days, or where the law in your country gives you a right to a refund.</p>

      <h2 class="t-h3">1-month pass: no refunds</h2>
      <p>The 1-month pass has no refunds, except a duplicate charge or a technical problem we can't fix. Lessons 0–2 of every course are free to try before you buy.</p>

      <h2 class="t-h3">How to ask</h2>
      <p>Email <a href={`mailto:${support.email}?subject=Refund`}>{support.email}</a> from the address on your account. Include your account email and the payment id. We reply within {support.responseTime}.</p>

      <h2 class="t-h3">How we refund</h2>
      <p>Approved refunds go back to the original payment method through our payment provider. They normally reach you within 5 to 7 business days of approval, depending on your bank.</p>
      <p>When we refund, paid access ends.</p>

      <h2 class="t-h3">Duplicate charges and technical problems</h2>
      <p>For either pass, we refund duplicate charges in full at any time. For a 12-month pass, we also refund in full at any time if we cannot give you access because of a fault on our side that we cannot fix within 7 days. For a 1-month pass, we refund in full for a technical problem we can't fix.</p>

      <h2 class="t-h3">Cancellation</h2>
      <p>Both the 12-month pass and the 1-month pass are prepaid, one-time payments with no automatic renewal, so there is no subscription to cancel. If you do not buy another pass, paid access ends on your pass's end date.</p>
      <p>Buying again before your pass ends adds the new period after the current end date. No days are lost. There is no upgrade credit.</p>

      <h2 class="t-h3">Your legal rights</h2>
      <p>Nothing on this page limits rights you have under the law where you live.</p>

      <h2 class="t-h3">Other policies</h2>
      <p>See <a href="/delivery/">Delivery and access</a> for when access starts and how long it lasts, and <a href="/terms/">Terms</a> for the rest of the agreement.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-head {
    padding-top: 96px;
    padding-bottom: 64px;
  }
  .legal {
    max-width: var(--text-max);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
  }
  .legal p,
  .legal li {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .flush {
    padding-top: 0;
  }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .page-head {
      padding-block: var(--space-12);
    }
  }
</style>
